			<div class="content" id="post-content-2277553">
									

<p>Ok, new one up! Thanks to MrWrong and Psygent for feedback on this. I'm kind of pulling the trigger on this now, because I need to stop fiddling around with it in my sandbox and work on my thesis.</p>
<p>Image credits: Original anthill photo was taken by Jim Kennedy under CC by 2.0, and is available here: <a href="https://www.flickr.com/photos/nature80020/14969387821/">https://www.flickr.com/photos/nature80020/14969387821/</a></p>
<p>It was overlain with an image of the east face painted hills of Oregon, licensed CC by-sa 3.0 by wikimedia user Finetooth and available here: <a href="http://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:East_face_painted_hills_panorama.jpg">http://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:East_face_painted_hills_panorama.jpg</a></p>
<p>The chart started life as a US Geological Survey chart of strata in Bryce canyon, and is under public domain, available here: <a href="http://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bryce_strat.jpg#filelinks">http://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bryce_strat.jpg#filelinks</a></p>
<p>Also, the broad idea behind SCP-XXXX-3 is an homage to a science fiction story I read some years ago about a strange subterrean geometric/metallic race and humanity discovering eachother tangentially, eventually resulting in the subterranean race killing all surface life by trying to visit. The races are otherwise not similar.</p>
<p>Edit: Now the inspiration of a concept album by Thetataurus, <a href="https://vreschen.bandcamp.com/album/debris-field">available here.</a></p>

